{#
  AGPL source offer. Running Loupe as a network service obliges the operator to
  offer the source it actually runs to the people using it over the network, and
  the UI is the only place those people are guaranteed to look — so this link is
  rendered on every page, signed in or out.

  The URL comes from the app_source_url Twig global (the APP_SOURCE_URL
  environment variable) rather than being hardcoded: an operator who modifies
  Loupe must point it at their own source, because a link to upstream would not
  offer users the code they are actually talking to.

  Props:
    class — classes applied to the anchor, so each layout styles its own footer.
#}
{% if app_source_url %}
    <a href="{{ app_source_url }}" class="{{ class }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <twig:ux:icon name="lucide:code-xml" class="w-3.5 h-3.5 shrink-0" />
        <span>{{ 'footer.source.label'|trans }}</span>
    </a>
{% endif %}
